{
  "repo": "microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat",
  "number": 5962,
  "title": "Add an opt-in ariaNotify() transport for screen reader announcements",
  "body": "> Part of `ariaNotify()`-first screen reader announcements (phase 1), related to #5857.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Added\n\n- 🧪 Added `styleOptions.assistiveTechnologyAnnouncementTransport` to announce via `ariaNotify()` instead of the live region, in PR [#5962](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/5962), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\nWeb Chat announces only via its live region, silent when the host hides it. With the experimental option set to `'aria-notify'` (default `'live-region'`), it calls `ariaNotify()` on its root instead, once per entry, falling back to the live region if unsupported.\n\n## Design\n\n- Text comes from the rendered entry (removed right after), so callers stay unchanged; `dom-accessibility-api` computes names, not live region text.\n- Next: a cancelable `webchat:announce` event, then `ariaNotify()` by default after an NVDA/JAWS pass.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `StyleOptions.ts`, `normalizeStyleOptions.ts` (+ spec): option, JSDoc, warns if invalid\n- `LiveRegionTwin`: cached support check, fallback, one call per new entry, empty live region\n- `getAnnouncementText.ts`: text walker\n- `ariaNotify/*.html`: calls on the root, empty live region, host hiding it, alt text, buttons, inputs, no repeats after switching, fallback\n\n<!-- For bugs, add the bug repro as a test. Otherwise, add tests to futureproof your work. -->\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [x] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [x] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
